From: acww-3ds <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Renderer 2D, game: the main screen kept on top (option ACWW_MAIN_TOP)

The 3DS port's option "Main screen on top" (options_3ds.c): while engine A shows the 3D, it stays on the top screen
whatever POWCNT1 bit 15 says, so the town and the rooms don't change screens when the pause menu opens. The pause
menu's opening and closing (src/main/unk_0206db88.cpp) then run on the bottom screen alone: the menu's background is
wiped in over the sky on the sub engine's window 1 instead of engine A's over the world (the host's wipe,
gpu2d_menu_wipe, takes the engine), and the camera doesn't lift the world off the screen (src/main/unk_0203a0cc.cpp),
so the top screen goes on as it is. The sky leaves the sub engine without being loaded onto engine A, where it isn't
shown (Sky_ParkOffSub, src/main/unk_020b8d9c.cpp: those loads were a hitch on the top screen); parked, its sprites
(the moon) aren't drawn, its palette isn't loaded onto engine A and engine A's backdrop keeps its colour, so the sky
on the top screen doesn't change. The background stays above the sky's layers (its stars at night) until they are
gone. The wide view's culling planes (src/main/unk_02039c08.cpp) lie 96 pixels beyond the picture's edges, so that
actors (the town gate) don't pop in at the top screen's edges.
